#AUTO 30
# PMIC (RK817) reachability + register snapshot over i2c0.
#
# Brings the i2c0 controller up bare-metal and reads the first 16
# registers of the RK817 PMIC (7-bit address 0x20). If the values
# come back as anything other than TIMEOUT, the PMIC is alive on
# the bus and we have a working I2C path to it — which unblocks
# reading regulator states, the battery fuel gauge, and power
# events later.
#
# All the work happens in C behind CALL pmic_dump (i2c0 bring-up +
# the Rockchip register-read transfer sequence); the probe language
# can't issue an I2C transaction by itself. Requires a kernel built
# with the pmic_dump CALL target (probe engine 019). If it logs
# "unknown target", reflash a newer kernel.
#
# Interpreting the register values needs the RK817 datasheet (not
# yet on hand) — this probe establishes the channel and captures a
# raw snapshot to decode against that datasheet later.

LOG RK817 PMIC dump over i2c0
CALL pmic_dump
LOG PMIC dump complete
